<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Destour</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Liberal Constitutional Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Destour ('Constitution'), formally the Liberal Constitutional Party, was a Tunisian nationalist party founded in 1920 by Abdelaziz Thâalbi and others. It demanded a constitution and an elected assembly under the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, but its cautious leadership drew mainly on the urban elite. In 1934 younger members led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habib-bourguiba">Habib Bourguiba</a> broke away to form the more popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-destour">Neo-Destour</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/destour.jpg" alt="Destour" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AkBY$ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandera_PLC_Nicaragua.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
